# PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

REGENT OF NORTH LAMPUNG

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF NORTH LAMPUNG REGENCY

NUMBER 1 OF 2017

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF NORTH LAMPUNG,

Considering:

a. that women and children have the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of torture or treatment that degrades human dignity, therefore they need to receive optimal legal protection;
b. that based on Article 9 paragraph (3) and paragraph (4), as well as Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, it is stated that women's empowerment and child protection are mandatory governmental affairs not related to basic services of the government and are the responsibility of the North Lampung Regency government;
c. that based on the considerations in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Women's Empowerment and Protection of Children from Acts of Violence.

In View of:







1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 28 of 1959 concerning Stipulation of Emergency Law Number 4 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1956 Number 55) and Emergency Law Number 6 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1956 Number 57) concerning Establishment of Level II Regions including Municipal Cities Within the Level I Region of South Sumatra as Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 73, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1821);
3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720;
7. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82 Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234;
8. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning Juvenile Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);
9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law number 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Regulations (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
10. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Domestic Violence Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604;
11. Government Regulation Number 9 of 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of Criminal Acts of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Women's Protection;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Child Protection;
14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence;
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;
18. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning Formation of Regional Legal Products.

With Joint Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF NORTH LAMPUNG REGENCY

and

REGENT OF NORTH LAMPUNG

DECIDES:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE.

